WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.600
LARRY P. ARNN: Our
speaker is Thomas Connor.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.940
He's known around here as "Doc."

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.530
He holds degrees
from Elizabethtown

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.630
in North Carolina, Chapel Hill.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:16.260
He is our most decorated
professor, this Professor

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.960
of the Year that I announced.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.150
He's won that four times.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.810
Nobody else has.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.360
Why?

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.130
Sometimes I think
he's like a grandpa

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.350
to them, and
sometimes like a dad.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.550
They flock to his
classes on the great wars

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.900
and on modern European history.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.280
They travel with him every year.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.510
maybe not this year--

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.220
probably couldn't go this year.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.790
He goes to battlefields,
and he walks them,

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.670
and he knows the story.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.190
And he takes them to cemeteries.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.590
I've been on one
of these things.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.350
And you go to the
American and the British--

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.120
those are the two best.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.870
He might like the
British a little better.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:57.200
I don't know, but
they're very good.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.908
And he's a critic of
these things, right?

00:00:58.908 --> 00:01:01.760
And the French and
the German, and he

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.099
has great reverence
for all of them.

00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:08.400
You walk around, and you
honor even the enemies

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.430
of the United States, who are
dead, who gave their lives.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:17.250
And then he can comment on the
differences of tone and shade,

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.180
which represent the
differences in the nation.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.845
From this experience,
he has written

00:01:22.845 --> 00:01:25.470
the authoritative history of the
United States Battle Monuments

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:26.782
Commission.

00:01:26.782 --> 00:01:29.940
And it is a solemn and
beautiful book to read.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:36.870
Senior class officers
wanted him because they

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.510
wanted this commencement,
the threatened

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:47.500
one, the interrupted one, to
be ours, just us family here.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.981
Welcome, Thomas Connor.

00:01:48.981 --> 00:01:51.927
[APPLAUSE]

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.950
THOMAS CONNER:
Thank you, Dr. Arnn.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:08.449
This is really a beautiful scene
and a beautiful moment as well.

00:02:08.449 --> 00:02:11.120
I think that heavenly
breeze is going to be

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.670
our salvation from the heat.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:17.990
And it would probably also add
10 or 15 yards to a Joe Phillip

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:18.815
field goal attempt.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:26.990
President Arnn, Chairman
Sajak, Chairman Brodbeck,

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:31.240
Class President Buchmann,
trustees, staff,

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.850
and faculty colleagues,
parents, friends, and guests

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:38.950
of the college, and,
most especially,

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.130
members of the
graduating class of 2020,

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:44.710
from both the undergraduate
college in the Graduate

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:49.440
School of Statesmanship,
this is the thrill

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.480
of a lifetime for me.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.990
And a thrill at my age can
be a very dangerous thing.

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:58.870
[CHUCKLES]

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:01.960
Nevertheless, I'm grateful
to the president, the class

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:06.720
officers, and many others
for the invitation to speak.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.330
And I'm especially
honored and humbled

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.780
for knowing that every one of
the three dozen commencement

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:17.070
speaker's who have played this
part during my service here

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:21.390
have surpassed me by wide
margins in either fame,

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:25.720
fortune, or both,
from Malcolm Forbes

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.560
and Russell Kirk in the
1980s, to Vice President Pence

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:33.280
and General Neller
most recently.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.420
But my good fortune has
exceeded theirs and at least

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.190
one respect.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:43.480
None of them has known
the incomparable joy

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:48.040
of spending their careers here
in the beautiful company of so

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.680
many that I have
shared for so long.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.600
Henry VIII was supposed to have
promised each of his wives,

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.920
don't worry, I'll only
keep you for a while.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.740
I'll only keep you for a while.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.950
Because I make you
the same promise,

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:14.800
I don't want to say another
word without doing two things.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.899
One is to extend my most
heartfelt congratulations

00:04:18.899 --> 00:04:24.610
to each one of the graduates on
your outstanding achievement.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.410
And because the mood
in the wider society

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:32.570
is so unhinged right now,
I want to urge each of you

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:37.010
in the strongest terms
never to let anyone,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:41.600
whether to your face or in
the media, cast aspersions

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.740
on the accomplishment we
celebrate today on the grounds

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:49.720
that you have been
unfairly privileged.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.420
There is nothing
inherently illegitimate.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:55.324
[APPLAUSE]

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:05.280
There is nothing inherently
illegitimate or abusive

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.140
to others about the individual
abilities you have cultivated

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:14.160
and refined, or the
hard work you've put in,

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.890
or the supportive home
environment your families have

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:19.530
worked so hard to
provide in order

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:24.452
to prepare you for the
rigors of higher education.

00:05:24.452 --> 00:05:28.730
The second thing I want
to do is to assure you

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.850
that the only thing
ending today--

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.190
there's a lot beginning.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:40.380
But the only thing ending is
your daily presence on campus.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.560
You will always remain
part of and have

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.620
an active claim
upon the fellowship

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:48.500
and the friendship
of this college.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.840
It's important that
you never forget that.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.720
We certainly find
ourselves in the midst

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:00.360
of a very tough stretch.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:05.510
For personal family reasons
and for far broader ones,

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.570
I would love to turn the
clock back to New Year's day

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:13.500
and give 2020 a second
chance or, for that matter,

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:18.330
as many chances as it might
take to produce something closer

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.510
to what our fondest hopes
imagined for the past five

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.650
months when the year began.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.360
Yet, amidst all the
disruptions, disappointments,

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:31.150
and dangers of
the recent months,

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:32.845
one reality looms large.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.190
Although we are in the
midst of a pandemic;

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:42.620
although domestic
peace has broken down,

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:45.820
especially in the streets
of our great cities;

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:49.750
although forces bent on
rewriting or repudiating

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.390
our history and tearing
down our livelihoods

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:56.900
and system of government
are running rampant;

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:59.510
although the promising
economy of February

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:05.370
has become the depressed economy
of March and April and beyond;

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.740
although some of you
may have forfeited

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.250
or had to defer
job opportunities

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:13.170
amidst the economic
chaos; although weddings

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:17.880
had to be postponed or modified;
although Hillsdale College had

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:22.320
to embrace universal online
instruction for a distressingly

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:27.290
long period of time; and
although the class of 2020

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:30.710
has had to make up,
in a single weekend,

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:33.050
for what should have been
closer to two full months

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.506
of celebratory activities--

00:07:35.506 --> 00:07:39.680
and you've done an admirable
job of that, I might add--

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.240
the world has not
really changed.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.430
I was drawn to this theme
for tonight's address

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:50.760
by recollections from the
last great national shock

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:55.860
that we all lived
through 9/11/2001.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.590
Many commentators
on that occasion

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:01.500
claimed that the attacks
in New York and Washington

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.650
had quote, "changed the world."

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.720
But I remember thinking,
even at that time,

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.670
that that wasn't true.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:14.660
The world had not changed when
the Twin Towers and those four

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.540
planes came crashing down.

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:23.450
Rather, what had changed was
our understanding of the world.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:26.900
We were forced, perhaps
some for the first time,

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.510
to realize that our
country was not completely

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:33.169
secure from murderous
attacks from abroad

00:08:33.169 --> 00:08:38.090
and that there was such a
thing as evil in the world.

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.450
We have been re-reminded
of those facts

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:44.179
continually in the current year.

00:08:44.179 --> 00:08:47.920
If it's not international
terrorists, but rather

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.120
tiny microbes trying
to kill us today,

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:56.040
we still confront
lethal dangers.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.320
And if the evil
stalking us appears

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:02.730
to be more homegrown in
2020 than the imported

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:07.200
violence of 2001, nobody
ever said that evil

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.850
can't come in many guises.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.900
All of these hard
realities and many others

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:20.330
too confirm what has been true
since the dawn of humankind.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:26.250
The world is fallen, filled
with danger, fraught with risk,

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.950
forever flawed.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:32.070
It is, in fact, a battleground
between good and evil.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:35.940
The battle won't end
until God's appointed time

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:40.970
and in accordance
with his eternal plan.

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:44.750
This world, moreover,
is not all there is.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:48.670
Nor, in the scheme of eternity,
is it our final destination.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:55.380
The whole of the Judeo-Christian
tradition affirms these things.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:58.080
And it is not within
human capacity

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.750
fundamentally to change them.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.450
Those who claim to have
a prescription for making

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.780
the world a perfect
place, by the way,

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:10.180
are the most dangerous
radicals of yesterday, today,

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:13.800
and tomorrow, all
richly deserving a place

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.210
on the ash heap of history.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:18.162
[APPLAUSE]

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:28.360
Well, if the cosmic
story can sound grim

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:32.800
and the worldly reality
is beset with troubles,

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.500
both are far from hopeless.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:41.750
There is plenty of goodness,
truth, and beauty in the world.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:46.940
And we know, as people of faith,
that God has willed all three

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:50.730
to triumph in the end.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:53.550
During the time that
we are given here,

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:57.840
it is our highest calling to
bear witness to these things

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:01.710
and to fight for them
with every breath.

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:05.820
Martin Luther put it this
way in his powerful hymn,

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:07.800
"A Mighty Fortress is Our God."

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:14.060
"And though this world
with devils filled

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:17.990
should threaten to
undo us, we shall not

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:23.270
fear for God has willed his
truth to triumph through us."

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.630
If it's important
for the graduates

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:30.780
not to succumb to
unrealistic hopes

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:34.020
as you begin the next
chapters of your life,

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:37.740
it is equally important
for you to gird yourselves

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:40.530
for what you can
and must contribute

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:43.110
to the right side
of the battle that

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:47.260
continues to define the nature
of the world and our purpose

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:47.760
in it.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.650
In this commencement
season, it is well

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:57.970
to remember that yours is
certainly not the first class

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:01.930
at Hillsdale College to
graduate into an unusually

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:05.630
turbulent and threatening world.

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:07.910
Imagine what any
of the graduating

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:11.000
classes during the
early 1860s must

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:15.950
have thought as they observed
the realities of the Civil War

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:17.510
and weighed how
they should steer

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:22.410
their lives through that
great national crisis.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:25.860
For the bulk of them, the
most immediate question

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:29.940
was how they could be useful in
the fight to abolish slavery.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:37.970
Imagine what the graduating
classes of 1917 and 1918

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:42.860
and 1941 through 1945
must have thought

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:46.430
as they braced themselves for
whatever part they would play

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:51.860
in the two great World Wars,
where human freedom and right

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:57.020
and decency also
hung in the balance.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:00.740
Imagine what the graduates
of a succession of classes

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:04.190
during the 1930s
must have thought,

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:06.800
as the worst economic
downturn in the nation's

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:12.300
history challenged and
restricted their options.

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:16.830
It is common knowledge around
here how Hillsdale graduates,

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:20.130
during the most famous
of our national crises,

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:23.520
rose to the challenges
of their times.

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:25.260
And it's no accident
that they did.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:32.330
You must be no different.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:38.520
Our hope and confidence are
that you will be no different.

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:41.700
Six of you have already chosen
and qualified for service

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:45.244
as officers in the United
States Marine Corps.

00:13:45.244 --> 00:13:48.136
[APPLAUSE]

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:57.230
Many of you will
pursue other kinds

00:13:57.230 --> 00:14:00.440
of military and public
service, further educational

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.930
opportunities,
teaching careers, jobs

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:08.580
in business and government, or
full-time roles in the home.

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:11.370
As we sit here, I
suspect that some of you

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:15.390
are unsure and perhaps,
anxious about what

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:18.435
you will be doing after this
milestone moment in your lives.

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:24.120
Well, take it from
someone who looks back

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:27.610
with sheer wonder
at how the nearly

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:34.420
50 years since his own college
graduation actually turned out.

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:39.280
You can't script a life.

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:41.440
It would take me
too long to recount

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.350
all of the unforeseen
and unforeseeable twists

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:50.800
and turns in my own career,
all the lucky breaks,

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:53.980
all the help I received
from mentors, colleagues,

00:14:53.980 --> 00:15:01.000
and friends, all the kicks
in the teeth along the way.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.910
None of us doubts
that each of you

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:07.320
will make your own
positive mark on the world.

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:13.070
God wants you to, and the
republic needs you to.

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.470
The simplest advice
I can give you

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:18.230
is always to be at your best.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:23.270
Learn what you can from every
experience, good and bad.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:27.020
Keep from doing and saying
foolish or idiotic things

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:27.965
on social media.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:33.530
Devote yourselves
to the right things.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.230
Pray without ceasing.

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:38.930
Be patient, and never give up.

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:47.610
The 15th day of next month
will mark the 75th anniversary

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:51.290
of the end of World War II.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:55.340
Japan, the last of our
enemies still standing,

00:15:55.340 --> 00:16:01.760
surrendered on August
15, 1945, VJ Day.

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:03.920
The end of history's
most murderous war

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:06.650
stands as the greatest
triumph of what

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:09.680
has been dubbed "the
greatest generation"

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:13.669
of our own national story.

00:16:13.669 --> 00:16:17.490
It's important to make
clear, in any case,

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:21.600
that we don't remember so fondly
and proudly the men and women

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:25.680
of the World War II era
as the greatest generation

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:29.340
because they rid
the world of evil,

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:33.240
because they didn't,
and they couldn't.

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:35.760
We give them special
honor because they

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:39.210
did destroy the evils
that most directly

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:43.290
and urgently threatened their
most valuable principles

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:46.350
and the nation that they loved.

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:50.370
They did what their
country required of them

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:54.280
without complaining
and without flinching.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:57.490
They won the battles that were
before them with God's help,

00:16:57.490 --> 00:17:02.910
just as President Roosevelt
vowed they would do.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:06.450
Once they had vindicated
the national cause

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:08.880
and helped to restore
tens of millions of people

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:13.560
all over the world to a life
of freedom and self-government,

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:16.829
they played the role of
citizen with the same selfless

00:17:16.829 --> 00:17:22.930
dedication and humility as they
had played the role of soldier.

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:27.880
This is why we celebrate
them and are made poorer

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:32.070
as they pass into eternity.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:35.810
God forbid that we
should ever forget them.

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:38.690
You need to be like them.

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:44.960
I submit to you that our country
thirsts for a new greatest

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:48.352
generation right now.

00:17:48.352 --> 00:17:51.280
[APPLAUSE]

00:17:56.660 --> 00:18:02.170
History has shown
before the threats

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:05.920
we face from abroad
and from within

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:09.880
and from a virus that
knows no borders.

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:12.820
Today's equivalent of
the Manhattan Project

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:17.200
may be Operation Warp Speed--

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:20.185
the race to come up with a
vaccine for the pandemic.

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:27.160
Familiar suspects continue to
threaten us from abroad as they

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:29.770
always have and always will.

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:32.980
The 21st century
Vandals and Huns

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:36.250
imperiling us from
within actually

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:42.440
speak English, in many cases,
college-educated English,

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:45.800
sometimes Ivy League English.

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:48.350
But the stakes could hardly
be higher if they screamed

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:49.910
at us in a foreign tongue.

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:55.600
The measure of greatness of any
generation of our countrymen

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:59.620
has always been how
well they stood up

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:01.720
to the threats
against their freedom

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:05.710
and the security of
their way of life.

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:10.720
What's distinctive
about today's dangers,

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:14.480
the ones you will have to
take the lead in overcoming,

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:18.310
is how insidious they are.

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:23.620
Recent polls and recent actions
are extremely troubling.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.900
Within your generation,
a recent poll

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:28.930
claimed 18- to
35-year-olds, that is,

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:36.090
only a minority, 35% to
40% assigned importance

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:41.430
to such vital elements as
religion or patriotism.

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:44.340
Within the 55 and
older age group,

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:46.860
2/3 claimed that
religion was important,

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:52.930
and 80% claimed that
patriotism was important.

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:54.820
In the midst of the
urban disturbances

00:19:54.820 --> 00:20:00.370
since the end of May, mostly
youthful crowds have burned

00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:04.000
and desecrating
churches and the flag,

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:07.120
defaced some of our most
revered national monuments,

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:12.380
and chanted that America
has never been great.

00:20:12.380 --> 00:20:14.450
Mount Rushmore, the
national anthem,

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:17.150
and the very idea
of Independence Day

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:20.920
have been disparaged
in the media.

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:23.940
A democratic
congresswoman insists

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.820
that the entire economic and
political system of the United

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:30.600
States needs to be torn
down in order to allow

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:34.530
for true fairness and equality.

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:36.960
What is so alarming
about this situation

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:41.280
is the compelling ignorance,
absence of sound discernment,

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:43.920
and lack of
historical perspective

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:46.110
on the part of those
who claim to show

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:49.500
the nation the path
to positive change,

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:54.870
all manifesting themselves
against the backdrop of such

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:59.080
a precipitous decline in
religious belief and love

00:20:59.080 --> 00:20:59.580
of country.

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:07.950
As the rising generation of
active citizens and leaders,

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:12.960
your ability to resist
this onslaught of darkness

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:17.040
and to preserve the republic
that is our common heritage

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:17.980
is going to be tested.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:23.900
The quality of your response
will depend, in large part,

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:29.960
on what you know, the value
you attach to what you know,

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:33.380
and the strength of
your own character.

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:38.250
Permit me, as one who is
quite aware of what you know,

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.090
to highlight some of the
most important elements

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:45.110
of this storehouse of
truth that must guide

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:48.890
and sustain you through what
will surely be critically

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:50.640
challenging times ahead.

00:21:53.340 --> 00:22:00.480
You know that every human life,
whatever the race or ethnicity,

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:05.040
age, or gender, born
or unborn, is precious

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:07.088
and deserves to be defended.

00:22:07.088 --> 00:22:10.076
[APPLAUSE]

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:23.200
None should ever be privileged
or advocated over others.

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:28.881
We are all made equally in the
image of God, and that's that.

00:22:28.881 --> 00:22:31.803
[APPLAUSE]

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.040
If all lives matter, you
know that livelihoods

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:40.080
matter as well.

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:44.730
You know that each of us bears
a duty to ourselves, to family,

00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:47.820
and to society to be
as enterprising as

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:51.540
possible with our
God-given abilities

00:22:51.540 --> 00:22:54.420
and with the skills and
talents we have developed

00:22:54.420 --> 00:22:57.770
with the help of others.

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:03.620
You know that human beings are,
by nature, social creatures

00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:07.160
and meant to live in community.

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:11.510
As the ancients and common
sense alike tell us,

00:23:11.510 --> 00:23:16.190
the family is the foundation of
society and the body politic.

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:20.030
Thus, you know that,
as families break down,

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:22.325
so will society and politics.

00:23:25.190 --> 00:23:25.810
You know--

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:28.720
[APPLAUSE]

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:35.600
you know that order is
the first need of all.

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:38.890
These are Russell Kirk's words.

00:23:38.890 --> 00:23:42.370
Authority, whether
public or parental,

00:23:42.370 --> 00:23:45.910
that cannot or will not keep
order within our various levels

00:23:45.910 --> 00:23:50.440
of community is not
worthy of the name.

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:53.860
You also know that the
foundation of politics

00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:59.650
in a republic is self-government
and that self-government begins

00:23:59.650 --> 00:24:04.000
with self and that, when
individuals habitually

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:09.010
yield to irrational disorderly
or destructive impulses,

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:12.900
community is impossible.

00:24:12.900 --> 00:24:17.390
You know that, just as it is
in the nature of human beings

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:22.480
to sin, nations
will do likewise.

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:26.050
But you also know that
the history of our country

00:24:26.050 --> 00:24:28.600
has been an ongoing
quest in keeping

00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:33.520
with our founding ideals
to correct and atone

00:24:33.520 --> 00:24:37.660
for our national sins and make
the imperfections of our union

00:24:37.660 --> 00:24:40.930
something closer to perfect.

00:24:40.930 --> 00:24:44.380
On this day, when a genuine hero
of the Civil Rights movement,

00:24:44.380 --> 00:24:48.040
John Lewis of
Georgia has died, it

00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:50.950
behooves us all to
rededicate ourselves

00:24:50.950 --> 00:24:55.994
to the continuing effort to
achieve true racial harmony.

00:24:55.994 --> 00:24:58.976
[APPLAUSE]

00:25:04.950 --> 00:25:08.925
You know, in all humility,
that the more you know

00:25:08.925 --> 00:25:14.070
doesn't necessarily make
you wiser or even smarter.

00:25:14.070 --> 00:25:17.040
Certainly, the endless
flood of data careening down

00:25:17.040 --> 00:25:19.290
the information
highway seems more

00:25:19.290 --> 00:25:24.850
to have multiplied
stupidity than reduced it.

00:25:24.850 --> 00:25:28.330
You know the need for
good faith discourse

00:25:28.330 --> 00:25:32.200
in the ongoing
competition of ideas.

00:25:32.200 --> 00:25:36.820
Rioting, cancellation, and
the dictation of angry mobs

00:25:36.820 --> 00:25:39.370
will never be
suitable substitutes

00:25:39.370 --> 00:25:41.950
for the honest and
reasoned debate that

00:25:41.950 --> 00:25:47.580
is supposed to be the glory
of democratic self-government.

00:25:47.580 --> 00:25:51.010
[APPLAUSE]

00:25:54.440 --> 00:25:59.480
You know further that more and
more distanced and remote ways

00:25:59.480 --> 00:26:01.130
of communicating
with one another

00:26:01.130 --> 00:26:04.460
and transacting
our affairs is not

00:26:04.460 --> 00:26:08.345
a prescription for a
healthier, stronger society.

00:26:11.500 --> 00:26:16.540
Most importantly, you
know that each one of us

00:26:16.540 --> 00:26:21.100
is beloved of the
God who created us

00:26:21.100 --> 00:26:24.040
and that this God
desires each one of us

00:26:24.040 --> 00:26:29.740
to pursue fellowship with him,
to serve him as our first love

00:26:29.740 --> 00:26:36.310
and allegiance, to trust him as
our ever-present help in need,

00:26:36.310 --> 00:26:39.760
and to acknowledge him as
the unshakable foundation

00:26:39.760 --> 00:26:42.730
of our being.

00:26:42.730 --> 00:26:45.070
As we contemplate the
parts we each will

00:26:45.070 --> 00:26:51.030
play in trying to set right as
much as we can in this world,

00:26:51.030 --> 00:26:55.080
more words from Luther's
already cited hymn remind us

00:26:55.080 --> 00:27:02.100
that we can accomplish no truly
good thing without God's help.

00:27:02.100 --> 00:27:05.100
And these words
also offer sure hope

00:27:05.100 --> 00:27:08.887
for how the great drama
we're all living will end.

00:27:08.887 --> 00:27:09.595
Here's the verse.

00:27:12.340 --> 00:27:16.330
"Did we in our own
strength confide,

00:27:16.330 --> 00:27:19.860
our striving would be losing?

00:27:19.860 --> 00:27:25.210
Were not the right man on our
side, the man of God's own

00:27:25.210 --> 00:27:27.590
choosing?

00:27:27.590 --> 00:27:30.110
Dost ask who that may be?

00:27:30.110 --> 00:27:33.070
Christ Jesus it is he.

00:27:33.070 --> 00:27:39.370
Lord Sabaoth, his name,
from age to age the same.

00:27:39.370 --> 00:27:40.750
And he must win the battle."

00:27:43.750 --> 00:27:50.050
If any of this preceding
litany has seemed self-evident

00:27:50.050 --> 00:27:53.980
or so commonly understood,
especially within this circle,

00:27:53.980 --> 00:27:58.540
as not to merit restating,
permit me to share with you

00:27:58.540 --> 00:28:01.690
a thought recently expressed
in a source sadly that I cannot

00:28:01.690 --> 00:28:06.770
recall, but which went
something like this.

00:28:06.770 --> 00:28:10.370
In times of trial, it
is the responsibility

00:28:10.370 --> 00:28:14.975
of every educated person
to belabor the obvious.

00:28:17.700 --> 00:28:19.920
This reminds us of
the advice coaches

00:28:19.920 --> 00:28:23.700
typically give to their teams
when the teams are struggling

00:28:23.700 --> 00:28:27.660
or when they're coming up
on a particularly big game.

00:28:27.660 --> 00:28:30.750
We've got to concentrate
on the fundamentals.

00:28:30.750 --> 00:28:34.530
We've got to get the
fundamentals right.

00:28:34.530 --> 00:28:39.110
Indeed, we do, perhaps
as never before.

00:28:39.110 --> 00:28:43.420
So in closing, I challenge
the graduates and all of us

00:28:43.420 --> 00:28:48.170
here to bring as much
as we possibly can

00:28:48.170 --> 00:28:53.570
of humanity, society,
decency, and dutifulness

00:28:53.570 --> 00:28:59.300
to past, present, and
future into our households,

00:28:59.300 --> 00:29:04.900
our places of work, and all
levels of our communities.

00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:07.740
Affirm the fundamentals.

00:29:07.740 --> 00:29:10.570
Seek the good.

00:29:10.570 --> 00:29:13.330
Be guided by the truth.

00:29:13.330 --> 00:29:15.340
What God has revealed
to us in his word

00:29:15.340 --> 00:29:18.990
and in the time-honored
wisdom of the ages.

00:29:18.990 --> 00:29:22.080
Love the beautiful.

00:29:22.080 --> 00:29:24.300
These have been the
foundational elements

00:29:24.300 --> 00:29:27.080
of your education here.

00:29:27.080 --> 00:29:30.930
Much of the world is
at odds with them.

00:29:30.930 --> 00:29:35.190
Your strength will rejoice
in the challenge of defending

00:29:35.190 --> 00:29:36.010
and promoting them.

00:29:38.890 --> 00:29:44.560
May God bless us everyone to
the task he's given us to do.

00:29:44.560 --> 00:29:49.630
May he always guide, protect,
and prosper the United States

00:29:49.630 --> 00:29:51.640
and this honorable college.

00:29:51.640 --> 00:29:52.480
Thank you.

00:29:52.480 --> 00:29:55.530
[APPLAUSE]

